r for `user_identity` [M]\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163749:**Size**: M (one new driver file; mirrors existing `memo_share.go` patterns).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163768:**Expected Outcome**: SQLite driver compiles and returns populated rows.\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163775:### T4: Implement Postgres driver for `user_identity` [M]\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163779:**Size**: M (one new driver file; mirrors `store/db/postgres/memo_share.go`).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163794:**Expected Outcome**: Postgres driver compiles.\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163801:### T5: Implement MySQL driver for `user_identity` [M]\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163803:**Objective**: Mirror T3/T4 for MySQL, using `LastInsertId()` + re-read pattern (MySQL's driver does not support `RETURNING`; design §2).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163805:**Size**: M (one new driver file; mirrors `store/db/mysql/memo_share.go`).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163808:- Create: `store/db/mysql/user_identity.go`\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163816:  - Same shape as T3, using backticked column names (`` `user_id` ``, `` `provider` ``, `` `extern_uid` ``) and `?` placeholders, matching the MySQL idiom used in `memo_share.go`.\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163822:**Expected Outcome**: MySQL driver compiles; full repo builds.\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163825:- `go build ./...` — expects PASS (entire repo compiles with all drivers satisfying the `Driver` interface introduced in T2).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163831:**Objective**: Exercise create + read paths plus the `(provider, extern_uid)` uniqueness guard across the active driver (G2).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/plan.md:163964:- Running PostgreSQL or MySQL integration tests locally (validation commands only cover SQLite, which is the default `DRIVER` in `store/test/store.go`).\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:164075:### 2. Add a dedicated store model and driver methods\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:164082:- `store/db/mysql/user_identity.go`\n./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:164115:Add a new migration version after `0.27` for SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MySQL. Update `LATEST.sql` for each backend to include the `user_identity` table and its `user_id` index.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174188:**Goal:** Let users write three more CEL constructs in the `filter` field — scalar `startsWith()`/`endsWith()` (case-insensitive), `matches(regex)`, and `all()` over tags (non-empty) — each compiled to SQL across SQLite/MySQL/Postgres.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174217:- LIKE patterns escape `%` `_` `\\`; only SQLite needs an explicit `ESCAPE '\\'` clause (Postgres/MySQL default the escape char to backslash, and patterns are passed as bound parameters so no SQL-literal backslash hazard).\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174355:\tdefault: // MySQL: default collation is case-insensitive; backslash is the default escape.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174588:\t\tregisterRegexpErr = msqlite.RegisterScalarFunction(\"regexp\", 2, func(_ *msqlite.FunctionContext, args []driver.Value) (driver.Value, error) {\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174796:\tcase DialectMySQL, DialectSQLite:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174797:\t\t// MySQL has a native REGEXP operator; SQLite uses the registered regexp() function.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174953:\tcase DialectMySQL:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175020:  (MySQL/SQLite). SQLite uses a Go-backed `regexp` function registered in\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175023:  per engine (Go RE2 on SQLite, POSIX ERE on Postgres, ICU on MySQL 8.0+), so\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175045:Run MySQL and Postgres suites to confirm the `all()` subqueries and regex operators render correctly:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175048:DRIVER=mysql    go test ./store/test/ -run 'TagsAll|Matches|StartsWith|EndsWith'\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175049:DRIVER=postgres go test ./store/test/ -run 'TagsAll|Matches|StartsWith|EndsWith'\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175052:Expected: PASS. (These require the project's standard test DB setup; if unavailable locally, rely on CI which runs all three drivers.)\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175069:- **Element reference:** the unqualified `value` column is produced by `json_each` (SQLite), the `JSON_TABLE(... COLUMNS (value ...))` (MySQL), and `elem(value)` (Postgres), so `elementPredicateSQL` is dialect-agnostic.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178718:fragment for the active dialect (SQLite / MySQL / Postgres). cel-go never\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178732:- Keep parity across SQLite, MySQL, and Postgres, with golden tests for each.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178769:  `memos_unicode_lower` function, Postgres uses `ILIKE`, MySQL relies on its\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178838:`col ILIKE $n`, MySQL `col LIKE ?`.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178879:- **MySQL:**\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178919:- **MySQL:** `col REGEXP ?`\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178930:  ERE; MySQL 8.0+ uses ICU. Portable patterns work everywhere; engine-specific\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178932:- ReDoS risk is low: RE2 (SQLite path) is linear-time; Postgres/MySQL POSIX\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178939:`store/db/{sqlite,mysql,postgres}/memo_filter_test.go` (and the attachment\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179278:- A file-backed IdP has no database ID and must never be passed to a driver update or delete operation.\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179346:database driver must provide equivalent transaction semantics for this narrow operation.\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179445:- Concurrent `GENERAL` updates and IdP deletion preserving the runtime authentication invariant across database drivers.\n./README.md:179480:- **Radical Simplicity** — Single Go binary, ~20MB Docker image. One command to deploy with SQLite, MySQL, or PostgreSQL.\n./.github/workflows/backend-tests.yml:180925:              # Run store tests for all drivers (sqlite, mysql, postgres)\n./.github/workflows/backend-tests.yml:180940:          DRIVER: ${{ matrix.test-group == 'store' && '' || 'sqlite' }}\n./.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml:181312:        - Database: SQLite / PostgreSQL / MySQL\n./AGENTS.md:181409:- Storage: SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL.\n./AGENTS.md:181417:- Add migrations for all database drivers when schema changes, and update each driver's `LATEST.sql`.\n./AGENTS.md:181429:go test -v ./store/...             # Store tests, including DB drivers via TestContainers\n./AGENTS.md:181462:| `store/` | Store facade, cache, migrations, driver interface |\n./AGENTS.md:181463:| 