15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174217:- LIKE patterns escape `%` `_` `\\`; only SQLite needs an explicit `ESCAPE '\\'` clause (Postgres/MySQL default the escape char to backslash, and patterns are passed as bound parameters so no SQL-literal backslash hazard).\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174355:\tdefault: // MySQL: default collation is case-insensitive; backslash is the default escape.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174588:\t\tregisterRegexpErr = msqlite.RegisterScalarFunction(\"regexp\", 2, func(_ *msqlite.FunctionContext, args []driver.Value) (driver.Value, error) {\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174796:\tcase DialectMySQL, DialectSQLite:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174797:\t\t// MySQL has a native REGEXP operator; SQLite uses the registered regexp() function.\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:174953:\tcase DialectMySQL:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175020:  (MySQL/SQLite). SQLite uses a Go-backed `regexp` function registered in\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175023:  per engine (Go RE2 on SQLite, POSIX ERE on Postgres, ICU on MySQL 8.0+), so\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175045:Run MySQL and Postgres suites to confirm the `all()` subqueries and regex operators render correctly:\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175048:DRIVER=mysql    go test ./store/test/ -run 'TagsAll|Matches|StartsWith|EndsWith'\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175049:DRIVER=postgres go test ./store/test/ -run 'TagsAll|Matches|StartsWith|EndsWith'\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175052:Expected: PASS. (These require the project's standard test DB setup; if unavailable locally, rely on CI which runs all three drivers.)\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion.md:175069:- **Element reference:** the unqualified `value` column is produced by `json_each` (SQLite), the `JSON_TABLE(... COLUMNS (value ...))` (MySQL), and `elem(value)` (Postgres), so `elementPredicateSQL` is dialect-agnostic.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178718:fragment for the active dialect (SQLite / MySQL / Postgres). cel-go never\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178732:- Keep parity across SQLite, MySQL, and Postgres, with golden tests for each.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178769:  `memos_unicode_lower` function, Postgres uses `ILIKE`, MySQL relies on its\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178838:`col ILIKE $n`, MySQL `col LIKE ?`.\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178879:- **MySQL:**\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178919:- **MySQL:** `col REGEXP ?`\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178930:  ERE; MySQL 8.0+ uses ICU. Portable patterns work everywhere; engine-specific\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178932:- ReDoS risk is low: RE2 (SQLite path) is linear-time; Postgres/MySQL POSIX\n./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-15-cel-filter-surface-expansion-design.md:178939:`store/db/{sqlite,mysql,postgres}/memo_filter_test.go` (and the attachment\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179278:- A file-backed IdP has no database ID and must never be passed to a driver update or delete operation.\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179346:database driver must provide equivalent transaction semantics for this narrow operation.\n./docs/configuration-provisioning.md:179445:- Concurrent `GENERAL` updates and IdP deletion preser